    <ShortDescription>
      A Cross-Platform GNU Privacy Guard Based Password Manager built on a Privacy‑First, Zero‑Knowledge Design.
    </ShortDescription>
    <LongDescription>
      Passwords is a secure, lightweight, and fully cross‑platform password manager that uses GNU Privacy Guard (GPG) for encryption operations. Every secret you store is encrypted locally on your device using strong, open‑standard cryptography. Nothing is uploaded, synced, or shared. The application follows a strict zero‑knowledge model: only you hold the keys, and only you can decrypt your data.
    </LongDescription>
